{"created": "2026-08-17T20:29:46.490562+00:00", "modified": "2026-08-17T20:29:46.705892+00:00", "id": 21985363, "conceptrecid": "21753404", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21985363", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.21753404", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21985363", "metadata": {"title": "AlecKriebel/Math: STC/JC sharp-boundary reproducibility v1.1.3", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21985363", "publication_date": "2026-08-17", "description": "<h1>Public release assets</h1>\n<p>The authoritative external release location is:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>tag: <code>stc-jc-sharp-boundary-v1.1.3</code></li>\n<li>release page: <a href=\"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/releases/tag/stc-jc-sharp-boundary-v1.1.3\">https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/releases/tag/stc-jc-sharp-boundary-v1.1.3</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>It is active only when <code>reproducibility/verify_public_release.py</code> returns\n<code>PUBLIC_RELEASE_VERIFIED</code>.  The release page then carries the exact eight\nnon-Git assets needed for a complete replay:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><code>stc_jc_sharp_boundary_reproducibility.tar.gz</code></li>\n<li><code>stc_jc_sharp_boundary_reproducibility.tar.gz.sha256</code></li>\n<li><code>RELEASE_ENVELOPE.json</code></li>\n<li><code>RELEASE_ASSET_SHA256SUMS</code></li>\n<li><code>FINAL_RELEASE_ENGINEERING_REPORT.md</code></li>\n<li><code>verify_quick.log</code></li>\n<li><code>verify_full.log</code></li>\n<li><code>verify_regenerate_all.log</code></li>\n</ol>\n<p><code>RELEASE_ENVELOPE.json</code> binds the immutable source commit, the deterministic\narchive, and all three clean-checkout transcripts.  The flat\n<code>RELEASE_ASSET_SHA256SUMS</code> covers the other seven downloaded assets by\nbasename, including the envelope, so this command works from one download\ndirectory:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">shasum -a 256 -c RELEASE_ASSET_SHA256SUMS\n</code></pre>\n<p>The manifest cannot contain its own digest and is therefore the downloaded\ntrust anchor; its hash is recorded in the machine-readable\n<code>PUBLIC_RELEASE_VERIFIED</code> verdict and final release transcript. A reader can\neither verify the annotated tagged source\ncheckout or download all eight assets and run the extracted-archive verifier\ndescribed in the engineering report.</p>\n<p>The files formerly stored directly under <code>release/</code> certified an older\n18-page manuscript. They are historical only and now live under\n<code>history/superseded_release_evidence/outcome_p_2026-08-13/</code>.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Alec Kriebel", "affiliation": null}], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/tree/stc-jc-sharp-boundary-v1.1.3", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "software", "scheme": "url"}], "version": "stc-jc-sharp-boundary-v1.1.3", "custom": {"code:codeRepository": "https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math"}, "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 8, "is_last": false, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "21753404"}}]}}, "title": "AlecKriebel/Math: STC/JC sharp-boundary reproducibility v1.1.3", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21985363", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21985363", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21985363?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21985363", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21985363", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.21985363", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21985363/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21753404", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21753404", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21753404", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.21753404", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21985363/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21985363/sequence/default", "file